Signal 1 — the similarity of the best chunk

  answerable    min 0.339   mean 0.524   max 0.606
  unanswerable  min 0.298   mean 0.474   max 0.605
  overlap:      10 unanswerable questions score at least as high as the worst answerable one
  the best possible threshold is 0.390, and it gets 62% right

Signal 2 — asking the model whether the excerpts answer it

  correct       20/24  83%
  answered when it should not have  0
  refused when it could have        4
      What was total revenue in 2024 Q3?
      What explanation does the company give for the Midwest fall?
      How many days notice is required before a price rise under MSC-2022-100?
      Which law governs the supplier agreements?

The scores overlap, so no threshold separates the two groups — and this is not
a tuning problem. Chapter 11 explained why: similarity ranks candidates against
each other, and something always ranks first.

Reading the retrieved text and asking whether it actually answers the question
is a different kind of signal, and it costs one extra call.
